WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.085 --> 00:00:12.827
The children and Mrs.

2
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:15.348
Darling were comforting Nana with pats and cuddles.

3
00:00:16.848 --> 00:00:18.949
Nana's stomach was upset from drinking Mr.

4
00:00:18.969 --> 00:00:19.789
Darling's medicine.

5
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.570
was only a joke," Mr.

6
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.210
Darling said.

7
00:00:27.511 --> 00:00:31.572
It was clear that nobody had any sympathy for him, and this upset him.

8
00:00:32.524 --> 00:00:34.306
"All you care about is that dog.

9
00:00:35.026 --> 00:00:36.347
What about my feelings?"

10
00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:37.528
he shouted.

11
00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:42.892
Then he said, "The proper place for a dog is tied up in the yard!"

12
00:00:44.013 --> 00:00:45.835
To prove his point, Mr.

13
00:00:45.855 --> 00:00:47.616
Darling dragged Nana from the nursery.

14
00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:52.280
He pulled her outside and chained her to a tree in the backyard.

15
00:00:54.041 --> 00:00:57.684
Suddenly ashamed, he sat down on the back steps and cried.

16
00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:00.747
He knew he had made a mistake, but Mr.

17
00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:01.928
Darling could not give in.

18
00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:06.066
He couldn't face his family if he had to admit that he was wrong.

19
00:01:07.547 --> 00:01:12.291
So, that night, Nana was left in the backyard, away from the nursery.

20
00:01:14.132 --> 00:01:15.714
Mrs. Darling put the kids to bed.

21
00:01:16.714 --> 00:01:18.756
They could all hear Nana barking outside.

22
00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:21.858
John whimpered, "Poor Nana.

23
00:01:22.279 --> 00:01:24.080
She sounds so unhappy."

24
00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:26.262
But Wendy was wiser.

25
00:01:26.282 --> 00:01:29.264
"That is not Nana's unhappy bark.

26
00:01:30.696 --> 00:01:33.077
It's how she barks when she smells danger."

27
00:01:33.097 --> 00:01:37.780
Mrs. Darling checked the nursery window to make sure it was properly shut.

28
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.902
"Oh, how I wish I weren't going to a dinner party tonight!"

29
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:43.583
she thought to herself.

30
00:01:44.624 --> 00:01:48.386
She was worried about leaving the children in the nursery without Nana to watch them.

31
00:01:48.406 --> 00:01:54.709
"The night lights will keep you from harm," she told the children.

32
00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.471
She tucked each child into bed.

33
00:01:58.391 --> 00:01:59.432
She sang each a song.

34
00:02:00.564 --> 00:02:04.647
She kissed them good night on their eyelids and, with that, she left the nursery.

35
00:02:06.649 --> 00:02:07.729
Then Mr.

36
00:02:07.749 --> 00:02:08.110
and Mrs.

37
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.831
Darling went out into the night.

38
00:02:10.912 --> 00:02:12.133
They didn't have far to go.

39
00:02:13.153 --> 00:02:17.437
The dinner party was at Number 27, only a few yards away from their house.

40
00:02:18.617 --> 00:02:21.780
It had been snowing, and they were the only people in the street.

41
00:02:23.161 --> 00:02:27.184
The stars shone down on the soft white covering of snow and on the couple.

42
00:02:28.088 --> 00:02:33.310
But as soon as the door of Number 27 closed behind them, the stars, who were friends of

43
00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:37.432
Peter Pan, whispered, "Go now, Peter!"

44
00:02:38.813 --> 00:02:42.594
Back in the nursery, Wendy, John, and Michael had fallen asleep.

45
00:02:43.835 --> 00:02:46.856
A bright light darted from one dresser drawer to another.

46
00:02:48.297 --> 00:02:49.717
It was not really a light, though.

47
00:02:50.918 --> 00:02:55.220
When it rested for a moment, you could see it was a fairy no larger than a hand.

48
00:02:57.292 --> 00:02:59.094
The fairy's name was Tinker Bell.

49
00:03:00.275 --> 00:03:04.398
A perfect miniature figure, she was beautifully dressed in a tiny leaf.

50
00:03:05.239 --> 00:03:08.081
She had found a way into the nursery to look for Peter's shadow.

51
00:03:09.782 --> 00:03:14.006
Suddenly the window blew open, and Peter flew into the nursery.

52
00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:19.150
"Tinker Bell," he called softly, "where are you?"

53
00:03:20.151 --> 00:03:25.035
He had carried the fairy part of the way from Neverland, and her fairy dust was still all

54
00:03:25.135 --> 00:03:25.856
over his hands.

55
00:03:26.816 --> 00:03:28.838
"Come and help me find my shadow!"

56
00:03:29.398 --> 00:03:29.979
Peter said.

57
00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.241
The ring of a tiny bell answered him.

58
00:03:34.282 --> 00:03:35.904
This was Tinker Bell's fairy language.

59
00:03:36.764 --> 00:03:42.809
When Tinker Bell explained that his shadow was in the dresser, Peter rummaged through all the drawers, spilling

60
00:03:42.949 --> 00:03:44.190
everything all over the floor.

61
00:03:45.632 --> 00:03:48.394
He made a terrible mess, but he didn't notice.

62
00:03:49.535 --> 00:03:54.019
He also didn't notice that he accidentally locked Tinker Bell in one of the drawers.

63
00:03:55.039 --> 00:03:57.205
Finally, Peter found his shadow.

64
00:03:58.085 --> 00:03:59.146
He was delighted.

65
00:04:00.046 --> 00:04:02.067
But how could he attach it to himself again?

66
00:04:03.488 --> 00:04:05.929
Peter put the shadow on the floor and lay down on it.

67
00:04:06.909 --> 00:04:08.450
But it wouldn't stick to his body.

68
00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.572
Next he tried to glue it on with soap from the bathroom.

69
00:04:13.172 --> 00:04:14.352
But this didn't work either.

70
00:04:15.313 --> 00:04:17.934
Frustrated, Peter sat down and cried.
